    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FDA boxed warning for a possible link with malignancy, though there is no firm evidence of one"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Steroid-sparing T-cell inhibitors for age two and older; may be used first-line with topical steroids, especially with steroid phobia or facial or flexural lesions; for short- or long-term use and maintenance"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Pimecrolimus for mild to moderate disease, tacrolimus for moderate to severe (more effective); applied 2 times a day. Proactive tacrolimus twice weekly on flare-prone areas reduces flares"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "No skin atrophy, so safe on face, eyelids, neck and groin. Transient burning or stinging is the most common adverse effect"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
